{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/89468-amazons-and-gender-sex","id":89468,"title":"Amazons and Gender/Sex","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-12T07:36:40-07:00","id":89468,"title":"Amazons and Gender/Sex","content":"So, this came up the other day among friends. Amazons serve only female Scions, but Scions with certain knacks and boons can be whatever gender and sex they damn well please (including any possible point on the intersex or transgender spectrum).<br /> <br /> So, what happens if a scion who already has amazon followers changes genders, or a scion changes genders to female and later seeks amazons as a birthright or for aid?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T13:48:43-07:00","id":89688,"title":"","content":"I think it partly depends on whether or not the Scion's nature is hidden from the amazons, at least in the second case. If they pretend to have been female all along, then I'd imagine that the amazons in question (assuming they don't catch the Scion out) would be fine with serving the Scion in question if they proved themselves worthy of it. In the first case, I really don't know. It'd probably depend on the Amazons, Scion, and player/ST in question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T15:21:43-07:00","id":89767,"title":"","content":"A bit of googling led me to <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caeneus\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> Greek myth where a women transformed into a man is mocked for having been originally a woman, despite being pretty successful by classical measure of Greek heroism/manliness.<br /> <br /> That would imply there as least some importance given to your original sex - though weather Amazons would agree with Centaurs, no clue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T12:18:23-07:00","id":92392,"title":"","content":"This does bring up an interesting point, also what if a scion is much like the Marvel Loki and to some degree Mythological Loki. A Shapeshifter who is Bisexual and Genderqueer. &quot;He&quot; identifies with either both or neither sex and being a shapeshifter is truly neither male or female. <br /> <br /> And considering birth gender is kinda ifffy....after all scions were born mortals and couldn't command any followers in the first place and that changed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-17T23:43:02-07:00","id":93274,"title":"","content":"So far, the only instance of a woman becoming a man (loosely) is a talk show episode where a hermaphrodite decided to have his female parts surgically removed. If an Amazon woman decided to become a man, (given the evidence of thought that Amazons consider men to be the inferior gender), I think they would see it as a betrayal, and banish him from their group, if not kill him outright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T14:29:54-07:00","id":94467,"title":"","content":"The Dude, it's worth pointing out that facts of gender/sex don't really matter. In this situation we're only considering what the Amazon's opinions are, I'm not sure they'd even accept genderqueer exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-19T17:08:37-07:00","id":94556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/89468-amazons-and-gender-sex?p=94467#post94467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dude, it's worth pointing out that facts of gender/sex don't really matter. In this situation we're only considering what the Amazon's opinions are, I'm not sure they'd even accept genderqueer exists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, pointing that out is more of questioning, do they accept individuals who are born male but define themselves as female, but than I thought about Genderqueer folks who either identify with both genders, or neither gender and how they would treat them. As far as not accepting the existence of them, I think when it comes to the Dodekatheon anything sex or gender related is acknowledged as existing, weather they accept it or not is another question entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T13:11:56-07:00","id":95895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/89468-amazons-and-gender-sex?p=94556#post94556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think when it comes to the Dodekatheon anything sex or gender related is acknowledged as existing</div> </div> </div> </div> Can you point to any myth or history text suggesting that. I don't really have any evidence saying otherwise but it doesn't quite fit what I think of the ancient Greeks - very strict gender roles, but different ones than the modern world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-21T14:09:19-07:00","id":95944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/89468-amazons-and-gender-sex?p=94556#post94556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, pointing that out is more of questioning, do they accept individuals who are born male but define themselves as female, but than I thought about Genderqueer folks who either identify with both genders, or neither gender and how they would treat them. As far as not accepting the existence of them, I think when it comes to the Dodekatheon anything sex or gender related is acknowledged as existing, weather they accept it or not is another question entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm of the opinion that it's up to the individual Amazon, but if you want a general opinion, then you might want to look into Tiresias and Hermaphroditus. I suspect that you'll have to end up making a call of your own, but it's a place to start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T02:49:24-07:00","id":96785,"title":"","content":"Given that Hermaphroditus is considered a god himself in his story, perhaps Scions can ask him themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T06:18:57-07:00","id":96847,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but which gods did Amazons follow?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T10:52:27-07:00","id":96941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/89468-amazons-and-gender-sex?p=96847#post96847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but which gods did Amazons follow?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the source, but it seems that the Amazons started out living close to the Scythians but relocated to Asia Minor at some point. So, I'd go with the Amazons worshiping either the Greek or the Scythian pantheon. Since the Scythians were one of the Iranian peoples, I'd substitute their pantheon with either the Yazatas or a mixture of figures from both the Yazatas and the Devas.<br /> <br /> Herodotus has a list of names for the Scythian pantheon, but there doesn't seem to be enough information to build an usable pantheon. Hence the substitution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1607,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","user":"Creticus","date":". 03-23-2014, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1607-creticus","name":"Creticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T12:47:48-07:00","id":97000,"title":"","content":"hmm...I recall reading that Apollo was the god of homosexuality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T15:02:34-07:00","id":97064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/89468-amazons-and-gender-sex?p=97000#post97000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hmm...I recall reading that Apollo was the god of homosexuality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the idea of someone being homosexual, heterosexual, bisexual, or anywhere inside, or outside, the incredibly large spectrum that exists, is a very modern idea. So, I highly doubt that Apollo was the patron of homosexuality. He may have been the patron of Pederasty, but I have seen of no mention of that in his Cult worship either at Delos or Delphi, or as a theme in his myths any more so than, say, Zeus has it. But, if you know where you read that Shadowflame, I would be very interested in looking into it, it'd be very interesting if true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T18:10:00-07:00","id":97152,"title":"","content":"It was a while back that I read it. I may have read misunderstood the article then...*shrugs*<br /> <br /> I see <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pederasty_in_ancient_Greece#In_myth_and_religion\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> that most of the major Greek gods were pederasts at one time or another. (Ares was too busy with the a certain goddess I suppose.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T20:32:53-07:00","id":97244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Creticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/89468-amazons-and-gender-sex?p=96941#post96941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends on the source, but it seems that the Amazons started out living close to the Scythians but relocated to Asia Minor at some point. So, I'd go with the Amazons worshiping either the Greek or the Scythian pantheon. Since the Scythians were one of the Iranian peoples, I'd substitute their pantheon with either the Yazatas or a mixture of figures from both the Yazatas and the Devas.<br /> <br /> Herodotus has a list of names for the Scythian pantheon, but there doesn't seem to be enough information to build an usable pantheon. Hence the substitution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bear in mind amazons as followers aren't pantheon-specific (<i>Scion: Hero</i> makes this clear) -- it just happens to be the amazons of Greek myth are the most visible, and for that reason the antagonist/background has that namesake. Though, given the write-up of them in the books I'd go on a limb and say they won't be following many male gods, if at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T01:15:09-07:00","id":98188,"title":"","content":"I think that Artemis was considered their patron goddess given her stance on the male gender. Of course, that may be just fiction plot and I don't really know what I'm talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T11:52:48-07:00","id":150657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/89468-amazons-and-gender-sex#post89468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this came up the other day among friends. Amazons serve only female Scions, but Scions with certain knacks and boons can be whatever gender and sex they damn well please (including any possible point on the intersex or transgender spectrum).<br /> <br /> So, what happens if a scion who already has amazon followers changes genders, or a scion changes genders to female and later seeks amazons as a birthright or for aid?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, in something that may surprise most modern readers, they seemed to be more connected with Ares, either directly - Hippolyta was his daughter - or indirectly (the centaurs, frequently associated/compared to them, descended of Ares through Ixion) than goddesses like Artemis or Athena. They were not very much into the greek &quot;tame &amp; limited&quot; sort of empowerment, while Ares loved all his children, good &amp; bad, male &amp; female, equally. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazons\" target=\"_blank\">references</a> for fun and profit.<br /> <br /> It all depends on how PC and ST want to play it up - i remember a scion of Legba that actually tricked his amazon followers in believing he was a female scion whose gender was changed by a curse and trying to get it undone. He also tricked them into believing it was to their mutual benefit to &quot;hack the curse&quot; by sex and using it to have powerful amazon children.<br /> <br /> What's no worse than a cheeky scion of Hel who would play seductive vampire lord for his seraglio of devoted jotunblut-empowered &quot;brides&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In the end what matters is that the PCs are scions and the amazons are not, so they should be capable of bending the rules, at least some of the time, if they have a good way to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-27-2014, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T12:16:50-07:00","id":150696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/89468-amazons-and-gender-sex?p=150657#post150657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It all depends on how PC and ST want to play it up - i remember a scion of Legba that actually tricked his amazon followers in believing he was a female scion whose gender was changed by a curse and trying to get it undone. He also tricked them into believing it was to their mutual benefit to &quot;hack the curse&quot; by sex and using it to have powerful amazon children.<br /> <br /> What's no worse than a cheeky scion of Hel who would play seductive vampire lord for his seraglio of devoted jotunblut-empowered &quot;brides&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, the incredibly fucked-up and horribly shady side of Epic Manipulation. One of the darker shades of gray in Scion and one I think my group actually forbid. Jotunblut-roofies are a no-no and probably getting you in huge trouble with the Aesir because it's effectively date-rape and the Norse had plenty of laws around the act of rape itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T12:31:26-07:00","id":150711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/89468-amazons-and-gender-sex?p=150696#post150696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, the incredibly fucked-up and horribly shady side of Epic Manipulation. One of the darker shades of gray in Scion and one I think my group actually forbid. Jotunblut-roofies are a no-no and probably getting you in huge trouble with the Aesir because it's effectively date-rape and the Norse had plenty of laws around the act of rape itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the guy was pretty light-hearted in a grim sort of way. It all started from him jotunblut-ing a fatebound hanger-on that had gotten in her head <b>already</b> that he was a vampire (bunch of incidents involving epic stamina, strength, death boons and a jacket that turns into wings) just so she was a little less defenseless and snowballing very, very fast. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T12:42:13-07:00","id":150720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/89468-amazons-and-gender-sex?p=150711#post150711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, the guy was pretty light-hearted in a grim sort of way. It all started from him jotunblut-ing a fatebound hanger-on that had gotten in her head <b>already</b> that he was a vampire (bunch of incidents involving epic stamina, strength, death boons and a jacket that turns into wings) just so she was a little less defenseless and snowballing very, very fast. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>....I really, really, really hope you're not implying that the date-rape via Jotunblut was her fault because then I'll have to drag over my soap-box and actually throw gender issues issues into this and the fact that mythology might be incredible misogynistic and filled to the brim with rape; but that groups shouldn't be going around acting like it's ok. I don't wanna do that, I'm in the middle of a semester break and would like to keep women's rights to college papers.<br /> <br /> But that Scion should have nasty consequences from his pantheon because the Norse had laws against this sort of thing. maybe not date-rape, but by feeding the girl Jotunblut essentially made her a servant and you don't abuse your servants.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T12:52:36-07:00","id":150729,"title":"","content":"Ancient Scandinavian laws indicate rape was punishable by outlawry. Outlawry means that anyone can murder you completely free from legal consequence. In some cases, particularly brutal instances of rape would proceed directly to the d<b>eath penalty</b>, and the loss of all titles and lands. The gods themselves might be considerably more intolerant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}